# Simple names

Always use short, common English words for files, classes, functions, methods, and DB columns.

## Do
- Prefer: `Product`, `addImage`, `stock_in`, `selling_price`
- One clear idea per name
- Match existing repo style (`snake_case` columns, `PascalCase` classes, `camelCase` methods)

## Do not
- Fancy or rare words (`orchestrate`, `hydrate`, `facade` as a custom name)
- Stacked jargon (`ProductVariantInventoryReconciliationService`)
- Unneeded prefixes/suffixes (`IProduct`, `ProductManagerHelperUtil`)

## When unsure
Pick the word a shop staff member would say out loud. If two words work, use the shorter one.
